Use your iOS simulator flow:

# build
dotnet build Codelingo.Frontend.csproj -f net10.0-ios
# boot simulator (only if not already running)
xcrun simctl boot 08CC77B8-6B2D-48A9-B9C8-E54C5E713DFB
xcrun simctl bootstatus 08CC77B8-6B2D-48A9-B9C8-E54C5E713DFB -b
# reinstall app
xcrun simctl uninstall 08CC77B8-6B2D-48A9-B9C8-E54C5E713DFB com.rudra.codelingo.frontend.new
xcrun simctl install 08CC77B8-6B2D-48A9-B9C8-E54C5E713DFB ./bin/Debug/net10.0-ios/iossimulator-arm64/Codelingo.Frontend.app
# launch
xcrun simctl launch 08CC77B8-6B2D-48A9-B9C8-E54C5E713DFB com.rudra.codelingo.frontend.new

⸻

If UI doesn’t update:

dotnet clean
dotnet build Codelingo.Frontend.csproj -f net10.0-ios